    "localmaxxing": {
      "backend": null,
      "hardware_label": "RTX 3080",
      "notes": "Gemma 4 12B IT QAT q4_0 (official Google GGUF, 6.50 GiB), 48 layers, ALL on GPU, fully resident at 32K in 7.47 GB. By far the best latency of the four models I measured on this card: TTFT 977 ms and 2699 tok/s prefill, against 2525 ms / 1080 tok/s for a 27B at 2-bit. Decode is within 2% of the 27B models while prefill is 2.5x faster, so for interactive and long-prompt work this is the better pick on 10GB. Gemma's 40 sliding-window layers cache only 1024 tokens; do not add --swa-full. Headless 3080 (both displays on the 7900X iGPU; desktop holds ~64 MiB on the card). Workload: single non-repetitive synthetic log-summarisation prompt, 256 output tokens, temp 0, cache_prompt off, medians of 3 reps (2 where noted). Prefill/decode from llama-server timings; TTFT measured client-side on a streaming request. Prompt token counts differ per model because tokenizers differ. llama.cpp b10472 (60eeeb608), Windows 11 / CUDA 12.4, driver 591.86, PCIe 4.0 x16, stock 370 W.",
      "observed_command": "llama-server -m gemma-4-12b-it-qat-q4_0.gguf -c 32768 -ngl 99 -fa on -ctk q8_0 -ctv q8_0 --parallel 1 --jinja --spec-type none",
